  "x-policy-resolution": {
    "source": "phase-loop-runtime/src/phase_loop_runtime/contracts/placement/vectors/policies.json",
    "accepted_names_at_this_version": [
      "minimal-with-app",
      "minimal-without-app",
      "full-remote-pi-runner"
    ],
    "rule": "policy_vector is a name, never an inline policy. A name in valid resolves to that vector's recorded digest, including while file status is pending_qualification. An unknown name, or a name in refused, refuses before any capacity probe or lease call. pending_qualification refuses a live coordinator connection, an image pull and any E2B call. Adding a name, renaming a name, or moving a name between valid and refused requires a new protocol artifact version. A status change belongs to ACTIVATE and repins this artifact.",
    "pi_runner_target_bindings": {
      "openshell": "full-remote-pi-runner",
      "local": "minimal-without-app",
      "e2b": "disabled"
    },
    "pi_runner_request": "A pi-runner ReserveRequest names full-remote-pi-runner as the ranked-workload policy profile. Before admission, the trusted target binding resolves an openshell attempt to that vector and a local attempt to minimal-without-app. The admitted Reservation is authoritative and records the actual resolved name and digest; no policy changes after admission.",
    "pi_runner_local": "The local admission uses minimal-without-app, returns bridge null, consumes one live_sandboxes slot before success, and remains subject to every shared local-headroom threshold. The reservation policy_vector and policy_digest name that resolved local vector."
  },
