  "x-placement-semantics": {
    "trusted_configuration": "The request contains no owner, client, target, target list, certificate selector, inline policy or fallback list. The required --client flag selects exactly one operator-owned configuration bound by config_sha256; the environment is ignored for selection.",
    "agent_and_executor_order": [
      "ai by authoritative capacity",
      "local only when every published headroom threshold admits",
      "e2b only after a later owner account-and-spend activation"
    ],
    "workload_rank_policy": "pi-runner is the only workload on agent_and_executor_order. leg, qualification and implementation are the existing seat workloads. For those three, reserve does not rank and does not probe. It admits only the single target already chosen by the landed SEATS JAILCORE route decision in trusted operator configuration. A missing decision refuses with sandbox_placement_workload_unsupported before any probe. An owned-host remote seat target also requires the current generic egress-and-credential probe receipt. A third-party seat target also requires that vendor's OD-7 record. The request carries no target, rank, certificate or route decision.",
    "reserve_idempotency": "The same request_id and the same canonical request body return the original response and do not create a second reservation. The same request_id with a different canonical body refuses with sandbox_placement_refused and creates nothing. Reap is not the retry path for one lost reserve response.",
    "release_binding": "release loads the stored reservation by reservation_id from the inventory selected by --client. A client mismatch or any supplied field that differs from the stored record refuses with sandbox_placement_refused, releases nothing and leaves the stored lease held. A repeated release of the same journaled reservation returns released while its tombstone remains, or unknown_reservation after tombstone expiry; neither state creates an admission barrier.",
    "outcomes_and_effects": "unreachable means a certain failure with nothing held. timeout means an effect may be held. A failure after a request may have been sent is timeout, never unreachable. Its barrier applies only to that reservation in the selected client inventory; it blocks later targets or retries for that reserve walk until release confirms the barrier, but never blocks another reservation, another client or the host.",
    "bridge_bytes": "For pi-runner on openshell the runtime creates one directory in its own state directory, mode 0700, containing one Unix socket, mode 0600. The socket is a bidirectional raw byte pipe of the admitted ForwardTcp stream. The toolkit keeps link framing, relay and credentials. The caller does not supply the path, service name, host or port. Every other reservation has bridge null.",
    "reap_scope_and_order": "reap examines only the inventory selected by --client and returns exactly one InventoryReapResult whose client and inventory match that selection. It can never inspect or mutate the other client's inventory. Within that inventory, eligible journal entries are attempted by created_at then reservation_id, max_items bounds attempts, and an uncertain item remains cleanup_pending without creating a host-wide or client-wide admission barrier.",
    "before_admission": "reserve may make a fresh admission attempt at each ranked target and records every attempt in trail. A typed at_capacity result authorizes only a new admission attempt.",
    "after_admission": "The reservation binds exactly one target and transport_id. The admitted launch envelope must name that transport_id. No route, transport, executable, environment, policy or deadline fallback is allowed after admission; a change requires a new envelope and a new reserve request_id.",
    "uncertain_cleanup": "A bare failure after a request may have taken effect blocks every later target of that reserve walk until release confirms its per-reservation, per-client barrier. Independent reservations continue.",
    "caller_context": "Opaque metadata echoed exactly and never used for identity, authority, routing, policy, correlation or launch input. It must contain no secret value or secret-derived digest.",
    "remote_writer_tier": "provider_readonly_patch_return_audit",
    "e2b": "Represented but disabled until ai is live and the owner supplies an account and spend cap."
  },
  "x-cross-process-vocabulary": {
    "placement": "Reserve trails and terminal placement results use AdmissionOutcome, AdmissionReason, CoordinatorErrorCode and PlacementCode only. TrailEntry.code is a required ResultCode, never null. A refusal before any target uses target preflight. seat_placement_waiting is a walk notice and is not a ResultCode.",
    "admission": "supervised_worker_cli admission uses AdmissionDiagnostic only; placement does not relabel admission failures.",
    "run": "Run status uses RunState and Termination. sandbox_placement_lost_after_launch and sandbox_placement_release_unconfirmed are attempt-evidence codes, not invented run states."
  },
